      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto, right margin",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Ibn Ya\u1e25y\u0101</li>\n<li>to please do this [for me]. I have requested</li>\n<li>the indigo</li>\n<li>\u2026 and the garments and the woolen cloaks</li>\n<li>and the hanbal (leather or fur garment). Let him leave this until, God willing,</li>\n<li>I arrive. M\u016bs\u0101 of Sfaqs is also carrying for me a sealed bag</li>\n<li>of coins which arrived from the West containing dinars ...</li>\n<li>If God decrees his safe arrival</li>\n<li>I would like my master to please take delivery of it from him.</li>\n<li>With him, I have also sent [a quantity] of olive oil. Please take delivery of everything.</li>\n<li>Similarly, I have sent with Ab\u016b \u02bfAl\u012b\u00a0</li>\n<li>\u1e24ass\u016bn b. Ya\u1e25y\u0101 two bags of coins: a bag of</li>\n<li>R\u016bm\u012b dinars and a bag of dinars from Tripoli, Syria and</li>\n<li>Egypt. If God decrees</li>\n<li>the safe arrival of all of these bags,</li>\n<li>and if you consider it desirable to sell,</li>\n<li>then please try to sell them.\u00a0</li>\n<li>Write me the weight of each bag</li>\n<li>and the separate amount that each one fetched.</li>\n<li>By this you will be doing me a favor. Also, let me know about the ...\u00a0</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 2
    },
